content.text:
I renamed `disableTooltip` to `hideHint` on `PillComponent` and its subclasses `app-fancy-pill` and `app-status-pill`, and `npx ngc -p tsconfig.json` reports no errors.

The rename covers:
- the declaration;
- bound and bare template bindings in `.html` files and inline templates;
- readers such as `fancyRef.hideHint()` and `this.firstPill()?.hideHint()`;
- `setInput("hideHint", …)` for pills;
- the `app-pill[hideHint]`, `app-fancy-pill[hideHint]` and `app-status-pill[hideHint]` selectors in `src/styles.css`.

I left `app-card`, `app-pill-legacy`, same-named fields on other classes, comments and text as they were. That includes the card's `setInput("disableTooltip", true)`.

I didn't read through the roughly 170 feature files line by line. My last grep for leftover `disableTooltip` on pill tags only matched `app-pill-legacy` lines, which are meant to stay.

